If you're running Gnome its nothing more than clicking

System -> Administration -> Synaptic

feed it your admin password

click Search - type in "nethack"

i chose nethack-gnome in my case (i'm running GDM).
let it install the dependencies too (click "mark")

then click Apply at the top

and voila all done :)

i can run it by pulling up a terminal and typing in "nethack-gnome"
i can run regular nethack by feeding it just "nethack"



